/T (All these different parameterizations of the conditional intensity function seek to capture and represent certain forms of dependency on the history in different ways: Poisson process makes the assumption that the duration is stationary; Hawkes process assumes that the influences from past events are linearly additive towards the current event; the Self-correcting process specifies a non-linear dependency over these past events; and autoregressive conditional duration model imposes a linear structure between successive inter-event durations.)
/E (All these different parameterizations of the conditional intensity function seek to capture and represent certain forms of dependency on the history in different ways: Poisson process makes the assumption that the duration is stationary; Hawkes process assumes that the influences from past events are linearly additive towards the current event; the Self-correcting process specifies a non-linear dependency over these past events; and autoregressive conditional duration model imposes a linear structure between successive inter-event durations.)
